title: Generalize @kv to schema-driven key/value types with optional get
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-10T05:18:42'
updated_at: '2026-06-13T09:59:06'
result: 'Generalized @kv to schema-driven key/value types with optional get. The store
  schema (fields named key/val) is now the single source of truth: kv_key_val_types()
  derives (key_ty, val_ty) defaulting String/i64, validates key==String and val in
  {i64,f64}, and gates incr/decr to integers. kv.get now returns Option of <val_ty>
  (built in the typer as a Ternary over KvHas producing Some(KvGet)/Nothing), so missing
  keys flow through ?/!!, else, and .unwrap_or rather than a sentinel 0. f64 values
  are supported via codegen bit-cast through the 8-byte slot (emit_kv_set/emit_kv_get
  reading store_defs); no runtime, HIR, or MIR signature changes needed. Updated 4
  existing kv integration tests to the new Option contract and added 3 conformance
  tests (missing-flows-else, unwrap_or, f64 schema). 417 integration + 27 error/access
  tests pass; zero warnings. Docs (store-improvement.md item 11, remediation.md) updated.'
description: Item 11. @kv key/value types inferred from declared fields (key as String,
  val as f64/String...); get typed as optional/fallible so missing keys flow through
  else, not sentinel 0. Schema is single source of truth for typer+codegen.
